  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Rob-41461baaeb33e9d7.mp3",
    "speaker": "Rob",
    "text": "Same three pieces, and both are questions. The first starts with \"is\": \"Is, not is, me?\" That means \"Is it me?\" The second starts with \"I\": \"I is, not is?\" That's \"Am I?\"",
    "duration": 14.8,
    "running_start_time": 105.32000000000004,
    "alignment": "Rob-41461baaeb33e9d7.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
    "gap_type": "turn",
    "source_id": null,
    "duration": 0.2,
    "running_start_time": 120.12000000000003
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Sunshine-15dcffdab72f4a03.mp3",
    "speaker": "Sunshine",
    "text": "[warmly] Yes! That 是不是 in the middle is the \"is it or isn't it\" question we met earlier. Put 我 at the end and you're asking \"Is it me?\" Put it at the front and you're asking about yourself: \"Am I, or am I not?\"",
    "duration": 16.08,
    "running_start_time": 120.32000000000004,
    "alignment": "Sunshine-15dcffdab72f4a03.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
